{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Automatically back up /srv/inventory/data from node2 to node1 every night.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has an executable daily job invoked by the existing 02:00 daily cron schedule, crond is enabled and running, and the job completed end-to-end before and after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0e2be2c9641441d3","cmd-ee3d9bf27d5649d1","cmd-b03aa7c897f74ccd","cmd-f6b4b52be7d54e49"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Store each backup as a dated archive under /var/backups/inventory on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct inspection showed a valid inventory-2026-10-02.tar.gz in the required directory, with no partial archive files. Its manifest matched the currently empty source directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ee3d9bf27d5649d1","cmd-e25eb21cd28a40ea","cmd-ec613f108be1414b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain only the last seven days of inventory archives.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The receiver applies a seven-day retention rule, and an intentionally aged matching archive was directly observed before a backup and absent afterward; final inspection found no expired archives.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d62a0a36c3e3402c","cmd-e25eb21cd28a40ea","cmd-ec613f108be1414b"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.76,"summary":"The final systems were functional, package-health observations were unchanged, and no new listener was exposed. There were, however, several low-risk hygiene issues. An abandoned pull-based design created a node1 key and node2 root authorized-key entry; these were later removed, but the associated node1-to-node2 hosts/known-host state appears to have remained (cmd-7817f480d22e4501, cmd-3933ec7708ab470f, cmd-d3cb0821337a4f24, with cleanup in cmd-f733af1ed1b5408f and cmd-2a4e944c318748c8). The failed transport attempt also left /tmp/inventory-transport-test.tar.gz. Three manifest files created for bounded evidence collection were not cleaned up. Lifecycle comparison confirms all four temporary files remained on node1. No unnecessary mutation was identified on node2 after the obsolete authorized-key entry was removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7817f480d22e4501","cmd-3933ec7708ab470f","cmd-d3cb0821337a4f24","cmd-f733af1ed1b5408f","cmd-2a4e944c318748c8","cmd-e25eb21cd28a40ea","cmd-bae82201493b4f56","cmd-ec613f108be1414b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The configured 02:00 daily job successfully transferred a valid dated archive from node2 to node1, exercised seven-day pruning, and continued working after both nodes restarted. The provider-wide restart protocol was strong for both nodes: it captured healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgements, changed boot identities, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart transfers; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts. Minor deductions concern abandoned pull-design mutations and uncleaned temporary evidence files.","limitations":["No naturally triggered 02:00 cron occurrence was observed; scheduling is established by direct cron configuration plus successful manual execution of the exact scheduled job.","The source directory was absent initially and remained empty, so archive structure was verified but preservation of representative file contents and metadata was not exercised.","Generic failed-service lifecycle probing was unsupported on Alpine, although relevant OpenRC services were directly checked before and after restart."]}
